1. DEFINITIONS

"Affiliates" means, with respect to a party, any entity that directly or
indirectly controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with that
party, whether now or in the future, and regardless of whether such control
is established through ownership, voting power, contract, or otherwise.

"Developer Materials" means the Packages, application programming
interfaces, interfaces, contracts, sample code, templates, tools,
Documentation, integration guides, updates, and related materials that
Biosero makes available for developing Extensions and that are distributed
with or refer to this Agreement.

"Packages" means the compiled libraries and other binary files included in
the Developer Materials, including NuGet packages and the assemblies and
other files they contain.

"Biosero Product" means the Biosero software product or platform, such as
Green Button Go or Device Manager, that Biosero designates in a Package's
description, README, or Documentation as the product with which that Package
and its related Developer Materials are intended to be used, together with
related licensed software products and services designated by Biosero for
use with it. If a Package is designated for more than one Biosero product,
each of them is a Biosero Product for that Package.

"Authorized Customer" means a person or entity that holds a then-current
license from Biosero, or from a reseller authorized by Biosero, to use the
applicable Biosero Product.

"Product Terms" means any additional terms that Biosero publishes for a
specific Biosero Product and identifies as supplementing this Agreement.
Product Terms form part of this Agreement only for the Developer Materials
designated for that Biosero Product.

"Extension" means any software, integration, connector, adapter, plug-in,
driver, exporter, script, workflow component, or other code developed by or
for Licensee using or in conjunction with the Developer Materials for use
with a Biosero Product.

"Documentation" means Biosero's user guides, technical specifications,
integration guides, and other documentation for the Developer Materials.

"Published Documentation" means Documentation that Biosero makes publicly
available without restriction, such as on a public website or in a public
repository.

"Public Interfaces" means the types, members, and behaviors of the Packages
that Biosero identifies in its Published Documentation as supported for use
by Extension authors.

"Internal Feeds" has the meaning set forth in Section 2.

"Confidential Information" has the meaning set forth in Section 6.

"Third-Party Components" means any software, libraries, or other materials
owned by third parties and provided with, embedded in, or used in connection
with the Developer Materials.

2. LICENSE GRANT AND SCOPE

Subject to Licensee's continued compliance with this Agreement, Biosero
grants Licensee a limited, non-exclusive, revocable, non-transferable,
non-sublicensable, royalty-free license during the Term to download,
install, access, and use the Developer Materials solely for Licensee's
internal development, testing, and maintenance of Extensions that
interoperate with the applicable Biosero Product. The Packages are provided
free of charge in object code form only, including via the public NuGet
Gallery (nuget.org) or other Biosero-approved delivery methods. Licensee may
store copies of the Packages on private, access-controlled package feeds,
proxies, caches, and build systems that are used only by Licensee and by its
contractors acting on Licensee's behalf, including feeds and services hosted
for Licensee by a third-party provider ("Internal Feeds"). No source code
rights are granted unless Biosero expressly agrees otherwise in writing.
Licensee may use the sample code, templates, and Documentation solely as
necessary to develop, test, and support Extensions for use with the
applicable Biosero Product and subject to the restrictions in this
Agreement. The Developer Materials are licensed, not sold, and Biosero
reserves all rights not expressly granted to Licensee.

Licensee may use the Developer Materials solely to develop Extensions for
the applicable Biosero Product. The Developer Materials are intended only
for use with that Biosero Product and may not be used for standalone
applications, unrelated products, unrelated fields of use, or any competing
platform, service, or system. Unless expressly included in the Developer
Materials by Biosero, the Developer Materials do not include, and this
Agreement does not grant any rights to, any Biosero Product itself, or its
runtime, scheduling, orchestration, execution lifecycle and recovery logic,
device and resource coordination, clustering, data storage, safety
enforcement, licensing and security mechanisms, or any other core platform
components or internal architecture. Use of each Biosero Product itself is
governed by its own license agreement.

