(b) copy, modify, adapt, translate, or create derivative works of the
    Developer Materials, except as expressly permitted for sample code,
    templates, and Documentation and only to the limited extent necessary to
    develop Extensions for the applicable Biosero Product;

(c) reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, decode, or otherwise attempt to
    derive source code, underlying ideas, algorithms, structures, or trade
    secrets from the Packages or any other Developer Materials, except to the
    extent such restriction is prohibited by applicable law and then only
    after prior written notice to Biosero;

(d) use the Developer Materials or any Biosero Confidential Information to
    infer, access, recreate, replicate, or compete with any Biosero Product
    or any other Biosero product or service;

(e) use the Developer Materials to build, enable, or support any competing
    laboratory automation, scheduling, orchestration, or device management
    platform, or any other offering or service that competes with a Biosero
    Product;

(f) re-implement, emulate, or circumvent any functionality, restrictions,
    interfaces, security controls, licensing mechanisms, or technical
    limitations of the Developer Materials or any Biosero Product;

(g) distribute, sublicense, lease, rent, lend, sell, transfer, disclose,
    publish, or otherwise make the Developer Materials available to any
    third party, including by uploading any Package to any public package
    feed, repository, or registry, or to any feed other than an Internal
    Feed, except as expressly permitted under Section 2 or Section 5;

(h) remove, alter, or obscure any copyright, trademark, patent, or other
    proprietary notices;

(i) white-label, rebrand, or misrepresent the Developer Materials or any
    Biosero platform-derived functionality as Licensee's own platform
    technology;

(j) use the Developer Materials in violation of any applicable law or
    regulation;

(k) use the Developer Materials, in whole or in part, to train, fine-tune,
    evaluate, benchmark, or otherwise develop or improve any artificial
    intelligence or machine learning model, or include them in any dataset
    used for such purposes, or submit or provide them to any artificial
    intelligence or machine learning service, tool, or provider that is
    permitted to retain them beyond processing Licensee's request or to use
    them to train or improve its models; or

(l) use the Developer Materials in any manner that exceeds the scope of
    Licensee's rights under this Agreement or any applicable Biosero Product
    license.

Nothing in Section 3(k) prohibits Licensee from using artificial
intelligence coding assistants or similar tools to develop, test, and
maintain Extensions in accordance with this Agreement, provided that the
tool's provider does not retain the Developer Materials beyond processing
Licensee's requests or use them to train or improve its models. Licensee is
responsible for any use of the Developer Materials by such tools on its
behalf as if that use were Licensee's own.

