unrelated use, or for use with competing products or services is granted.
Licensee shall not sublicense the Developer Materials. Any distribution or
transfer not expressly permitted by this Section is void.

6. CONFIDENTIALITY

"Confidential Information" means any non-public materials and information
that Biosero discloses or makes available to Licensee in connection with
this Agreement, including pre-release or privately distributed Developer
Materials, non-public Documentation, non-public APIs, non-public benchmark,
test, or performance information relating to the Developer Materials or any
Biosero Product, and other non-public technical, business, or product
information. Developer Materials that Biosero makes publicly available,
including publicly released Packages, Published Documentation, and Public
Interfaces, are not Confidential Information, although they remain subject
to Biosero's intellectual property rights and to all other terms of this
Agreement, including the restrictions in Section 3.

Licensee shall protect Biosero Confidential Information using at least the
same degree of care it uses to protect its own similar confidential
information, but not less than a reasonable degree of care, and shall use
Biosero Confidential Information solely as necessary to exercise its rights
and perform its obligations under this Agreement. Licensee shall not disclose
Biosero Confidential Information to any third party except to its employees
and contractors who have a need to know for the permitted purposes and who
are bound by written confidentiality obligations at least as protective as
those in this Agreement. Licensee shall not publish or disclose any
benchmark, test, or performance results relating to the Developer Materials
or any Biosero Product without Biosero's prior written consent.

The obligations in this Section do not apply to information that Licensee can
demonstrate by written records: (a) is or becomes publicly available through
no breach of this Agreement; (b) was lawfully known to Licensee without
restriction before disclosure by Biosero; (c) is lawfully received by
Licensee from a third party without breach of any duty; or (d) is
independently developed by Licensee without use of or reference to Biosero
Confidential Information. If Licensee is required by law to disclose Biosero
Confidential Information, Licensee shall, to the extent legally permitted,
provide Biosero with prompt prior notice and reasonable assistance to seek
confidential treatment or other protective measures.

