or otherwise verify Licensee's compliance with this Agreement, including
Licensee's use, distribution, and handling of the Developer Materials,
solely to confirm compliance and not more often than once annually unless
Biosero reasonably suspects a material breach. Licensee shall cooperate
reasonably with any such audit. If Biosero reasonably determines that
Licensee has exceeded or violated its rights under this Agreement, Licensee
shall promptly cure the noncompliance, if curable, cease any non-compliant
use or distribution immediately, and, upon request, provide a written
certification signed by an authorized officer describing the corrective
actions taken. In the case of material noncompliance, Licensee shall
reimburse Biosero for its reasonable costs of investigation, audit,
remediation, and enforcement, and Biosero may suspend any access to the
Developer Materials or Confidential Information that Biosero controls and
exercise any other rights or remedies available under this Agreement or
applicable law.

