12. TERM AND TERMINATION

This Agreement begins on the date Licensee first accepts it or first
downloads, installs, restores, accesses, or uses any Developer Materials,
whichever occurs first, and continues until terminated (the "Term").

Biosero may terminate this Agreement immediately upon written notice if
Licensee breaches Section 2 or Section 3, misuses Biosero intellectual
property, breaches the confidentiality obligations in Section 6, engages in
competitive misuse, circumvention, unauthorized distribution, or other
material misuse of the Developer Materials, or if continued performance
would cause Biosero to violate law. For any other breach, Biosero may
terminate this Agreement if Licensee fails to cure such breach within ten
(10) days after receiving written notice. Licensee may terminate this
Agreement at any time by ceasing all use of the Developer Materials and
destroying all copies of the Developer Materials and Biosero Confidential
Information in its possession or control.

Upon any expiration or termination of this Agreement, all rights granted to
Licensee immediately cease, and Licensee shall immediately stop all use of
the Developer Materials, stop all development and distribution of
Extensions, and promptly destroy or permanently delete all copies of the
Packages (including copies on Internal Feeds), all other Developer Materials
other than Published Documentation, and all Biosero Confidential
Information, except for archival copies required by law. Termination does
not affect the right of an Authorized Customer to continue using, under its
own Biosero Product license, copies of an Extension that Licensee lawfully
delivered to it before termination, unless that Extension itself breaches
this Agreement or Biosero reasonably determines that its continued use
creates a security, safety, or legal risk.

Sections 1, 3, 4, 5(c), 5(d), 6, 7, 9, 10, 11, 12, and 13, and any other
provisions that by their nature should survive, survive any expiration or
termination of this Agreement.

